Version 2.30, October 10, 1995

1/10/96  Added iso646.h header file

The iso646.h header has been added.  It defines macros for the alternative
spellings (e.g., bitand, bitor) for certain operators as specified in
Normative Addendum 1 of the ISO C standard.

12/1/95  Remove include of iostream.h from assert.h

The assert.h include file was changed to use stdio.h instead of iostream.h.
This change was made to reduce the number of header files that are pulled
in by assert.h.  Strictly speaking, assert.h should not include anything
else.  A "real" library will need to do assert.h differently.

9/1/95   Changes for namespaces

typeinfo.h, stdexcept.h, new.h, and exception.h have been changed to
put standard types in namespace std, but only if the front-end flag
RUNTIME_USES_NAMESPACES is set to TRUE.

When the runtime uses namespaces, the front end will define a
preprocessing flag (named __EDG_IMPLICIT_USING_STD by default) that
will be TRUE if the --using_std option was specified when the front
end was invoked.  The runtime tests this flag and does a "using
namespace std" directive when it is set.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.29, May 24, 1995

5/4/95   C++ standard header files: typeinfo.h, exception.h, stdexcept.h

typeinfo.h and stdexcept.h have been added.  exception.h has been
modified to reflect changes in the working paper.  The runtime library
source depends on the class definitions specified in these files.
Changes to these files will probably require corresponding changes
in the runtime library and vice-versa.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.28, March 2, 1995

2/27/95  errno.h: extern on errno

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.27, December 22, 1994

12/4/94  stdarg.h: va_end redefined not to be empty

11/21/94 stddef.h: ptrdiff_t redefined as int (instead of long).

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.25, August 19, 1994

8/12/94  exception.h added

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.22, February 26, 1994

1/27/94  toupper/tolower made inline in C++

The toupper and tolower macros in <ctype.h> have been made inline functions
in C++.  In C, the temporaries used by the macros have been changed back
to external (to avoid warnings about unused static variables when compiling
preprocessed output).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.21, December 21, 1993

11/18/93 struct __iobuf renamed _iobuf in <stdio.h>

11/16/93 toupper/tolower temps made static

The temporary variables used by toupper and tolower to avoid evaluating
the argument twice have been made static to avoid problems with the change
that makes declarations that are tentative definitions in C be true
definitions in C++.

11/15/93 Size of setjmp buffer

The setjmp buffer in setjmp.h has been changed to match the size of the
buffer used by SunOS 4.1.2.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.20, November 4, 1993

11/04/93 Exit function has C++ linkage

The exit function has been changed to have C++ linkage.  A version of
exit is now supplied with the C++ runtime to support exception handling.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version 2.09, September 15, 1992

9/13/92  stdarg.h updated for sparc architecture.
